where would you put yourself?

00:38:01.331 --> 00:38:06.331
- I Would say it's Ohara,
you, Chris, me, Garnt, Luke.

00:38:06.579 --> 00:38:11.579
- Yeah. I've no issue doing
black slopes or whatever.

00:38:11.615 --> 00:38:13.722
So me and Ohara cause we were
like the most confident ones

00:38:13.722 --> 00:38:14.555
we were like, all right,

00:38:14.555 --> 00:38:15.729
I was like, you go in the front,

00:38:15.729 --> 00:38:18.048
you like direct them
and I'll go in the back.

00:38:18.048 --> 00:38:21.742
And I'll, if they fall over,
I'll help them get back up.

00:38:21.742 --> 00:38:24.573
Luckily I'm glad I was there
'cause Luke at one point

00:38:24.573 --> 00:38:27.472
lost his ski in like really thick snow.

00:38:27.472 --> 00:38:28.791
And when you're in ski boots,

00:38:28.791 --> 00:38:29.944
you can't really go up the mountain

00:38:29.944 --> 00:38:31.707
if you're not used to it.

00:38:31.707 --> 00:38:33.986
If you're like a
beginner, it's really hard

00:38:33.986 --> 00:38:37.345
to feel confident running
around in the ski boots.

00:38:37.345 --> 00:38:38.699
And I was wearing snowboard
boots. So I was like,

00:38:38.699 --> 00:38:39.532
"All right, just wait there,

00:38:39.532 --> 00:38:41.148
"I'll go and dig through the snow."

00:38:41.148 --> 00:38:42.135
And after like five minutes,

00:38:42.135 --> 00:38:45.560
I managed to find this
ski buried in the snow.

00:38:45.560 --> 00:38:48.404
It'd gone underneath the snow
slid. So you couldn't even,

00:38:48.404 --> 00:38:50.880
there was no sign that
it was ship was there.

00:38:50.880 --> 00:38:53.608
So I had to like rummage through
yeah. Eventually found it.

00:38:53.608 --> 00:38:55.304
So we went down anyway, but like,

00:38:55.304 --> 00:38:57.433
so we took these guys up
and it was just a mess.

00:38:57.433 --> 00:38:59.868
'Cause like none of them
could like stand up.

00:38:59.868 --> 00:39:02.267
Chris is good at skiing,
but Chris is lazy.

00:39:02.267 --> 00:39:03.663
(Garnt laughs)

00:39:03.663 --> 00:39:05.443
- I did notice that. I did notice that.

00:39:05.443 --> 00:39:08.464
- Chris, Ken, and I reckon
Chris could probably do

00:39:08.464 --> 00:39:09.592
a black slope, right?

00:39:09.592 --> 00:39:10.425
- Yeah.

00:39:10.425 --> 00:39:12.512
- Maybe. If Chris really tried.

00:39:12.512 --> 00:39:14.112
Problem is black slopes are really tiring

00:39:14.112 --> 00:39:15.584
and take a lot of effort.

00:39:15.584 --> 00:39:17.895
Chris doesn't wanna do that.
Like Chris also is like,

00:39:17.895 --> 00:39:20.103
he'll do reds, but you
really have to convince him.

00:39:20.103 --> 00:39:20.994
You're supposed to do greens.

00:39:20.994 --> 00:39:23.214
It's like Chris, you
could do reds so easily.

00:39:23.214 --> 00:39:24.047
What are you doing?

00:39:24.047 --> 00:39:25.774
- Yeah. Because I remember
like the third or fourth day

00:39:25.774 --> 00:39:28.073
he came with me, Garnt,
and Luke on a green slope

00:39:28.073 --> 00:39:30.222
'cause that's when we started
to get a little more confident

00:39:30.222 --> 00:39:32.104
and he was like, "Yeah, I think
I'll stick on a green too."

00:39:32.104 --> 00:39:33.036
And I'm like--

00:39:33.036 --> 00:39:35.187
- Fuck off here, get outta here,

00:39:35.187 --> 00:39:37.179
you passed the exam go away.

00:39:37.179 --> 00:39:40.070
- And he's like skiing past
us with no problem whatsoever

00:39:40.070 --> 00:39:42.338
being like, "Come on,
boys, catch up boys."

00:39:42.338 --> 00:39:43.419
I'm like fuck off.

00:39:43.419 --> 00:39:44.286
(all laughing)

00:39:44.286 --> 00:39:47.567
- Cause yeah. So, the second
day we tried to take them down

00:39:47.567 --> 00:39:49.373
How long did it take us to get to them?

00:39:49.373 --> 00:39:52.829
Okay. So if I went from top
to bottom without stopping

00:39:52.829 --> 00:39:53.869
and I went as fast as I could,

00:39:53.869 --> 00:39:55.171
I could probably do it
in five minutes. Right?

00:39:55.171 --> 00:39:56.004
- Yeah.

00:39:56.004 --> 00:39:56.837
- But that's like didn't
do initially fast--

00:39:56.837 --> 00:39:59.916
- Well, it probably took
us 30 to 45 Minutes.

00:39:59.916 --> 00:40:01.550
- No, it took us like second hour.

00:40:01.550 --> 00:40:02.383
- Really?

00:40:02.383 --> 00:40:03.216
- It took like the two hours.

00:40:03.216 --> 00:40:04.252
- The first time at least.

00:40:04.252 --> 00:40:05.085
- Oh. The first time, yeah, yeah.

00:40:05.085 --> 00:40:08.303
Because after it I swear we
spent like 15 to 20 minutes

00:40:08.303 --> 00:40:11.315
looking for, well you were
looking for Luke's skis.

00:40:11.315 --> 00:40:13.796
And then before that as well,

00:40:13.796 --> 00:40:15.393
because this was right at the start.

00:40:15.393 --> 00:40:17.393
So the visibility was so poor.

00:40:17.393 --> 00:40:19.729
I probably would have
a hard time seeing Joey

00:40:19.729 --> 00:40:21.114
from where he is sitting.

00:40:21.114 --> 00:40:23.151
That's how poor the visibility was.

00:40:23.151 --> 00:40:26.394
And this was also
basically my only my second

00:40:26.394 --> 00:40:28.695
four-day skiing. So snowboarding.

00:40:28.695 --> 00:40:32.936
So I didn't know how to
properly control my board.

00:40:32.936 --> 00:40:35.108
And I remember we were trying
to stick close to a group.

00:40:35.108 --> 00:40:36.873
We were trying to stick close
to a group and I'm trying like

00:40:36.873 --> 00:40:40.598
I'm fighting for life. Just
like see where the group was.

00:40:40.598 --> 00:40:44.727
And so before every hill,
we all stop before a hill.

00:40:44.727 --> 00:40:47.847
Unfortunately my control of
the board was not good enough

00:40:47.847 --> 00:40:50.058
that I knew how to stop yet.

00:40:50.058 --> 00:40:53.257
So these guys were stopped
waiting for me and Luke.

00:40:53.257 --> 00:40:57.024
And so I come along and I
try to stop and I realized

00:40:57.024 --> 00:41:00.264
that I am stopping too late
and I'm sliding down the slope.

00:41:00.264 --> 00:41:03.482
So I start shouting out, "Oh
guys, oh, I'm going down.

00:41:03.482 --> 00:41:04.724
"I'm just gonna go ahead."

00:41:04.724 --> 00:41:06.557
And nobody looked back

00:41:09.064 --> 00:41:12.814
and I just start stumbling down
this hill, get halfway down.

00:41:12.814 --> 00:41:15.246
And I turn around to see
if anyone's followed,

00:41:15.246 --> 00:41:19.004
wait a minute, wait two
minutes, wait five minutes.

00:41:19.004 --> 00:41:22.757
It's there's nobody. And I'm
just like, where is everybody?

00:41:22.757 --> 00:41:26.838
I am on this slope at the top
of this mountain by myself

00:41:26.838 --> 00:41:29.452
and I can't even stop
correctly. So I had to like,

00:41:29.452 --> 00:41:30.984
I was like messaging the lion group,

00:41:30.984 --> 00:41:32.325
trying to get their attention.

00:41:32.325 --> 00:41:36.284
Luckily, I waited long enough
for you guys to come down.

00:41:36.284 --> 00:41:38.275
'Cause these guys were waiting
for me this entire time.

00:41:38.275 --> 00:41:41.024
- Yeah. They thought
that Garnt was behind us.

00:41:41.024 --> 00:41:43.523
- That's how poor the visibility was.

00:41:43.523 --> 00:41:45.147
So yeah, we wait just 20 minutes

00:41:45.147 --> 00:41:46.803
where you were waiting
for me and I was waiting

00:41:46.803 --> 00:41:49.510
for you just because we
couldn't see each other.

00:41:49.510 --> 00:41:50.592
- 'Cause I was really worried

00:41:50.592 --> 00:41:52.666
'cause the way that this
mountain was laid out

00:41:52.666 --> 00:41:57.165
is that basically you
have to do really big Ss

00:41:57.165 --> 00:41:58.793
to stay on the easy ones.

00:41:58.793 --> 00:42:01.125
And if they took any turn at any point,

00:42:01.125 --> 00:42:02.436
they have to go down a black slope.

00:42:02.436 --> 00:42:03.269
- It's just a cliff.

00:42:03.269 --> 00:42:05.066
- And I was like, they're gonna die

00:42:05.066 --> 00:42:06.685
if they go down a black slope.

00:42:06.685 --> 00:42:08.827
So I was like, I gotta
do my best to make sure,

00:42:08.827 --> 00:42:11.696
we got I'm like, like what
are they, what are they,

00:42:11.696 --> 00:42:15.254
what are the sheep dogs like
turn around up all the sheep.

00:42:15.254 --> 00:42:17.623
I'm like, come on, boys,
let's stick together.

00:42:17.623 --> 00:42:19.332
- Yeah. It was kind of like that.

00:42:19.332 --> 00:42:21.614
So which is why I think I
learned the most on the last day,

00:42:21.614 --> 00:42:25.454
because on the last day we
just found like this one slope

00:42:25.454 --> 00:42:28.664
that was perfect for beginners
and had like a ski lift,

00:42:28.664 --> 00:42:29.799
take us back up.

00:42:29.799 --> 00:42:32.789
And you just had like the
freedom to just do what you want

00:42:32.789 --> 00:42:36.516
without worry about dying
or just breaking bones.

00:42:36.516 --> 00:42:38.701
- Also the weather was
absolutely gorgeous.

00:42:38.701 --> 00:42:39.711
- [Garnt] And the weather was like--

00:42:39.711 --> 00:42:43.174
- Yeah. So we had three
days of God, awful weather.

00:42:43.174 --> 00:42:44.258
Really bad weather.

00:42:44.258 --> 00:42:47.415
And finally the last day we
were leaving, it was amazing.

00:42:47.415 --> 00:42:48.248
And it was a shame really.

00:42:48.248 --> 00:42:50.316
'Cause the next few days after
that were also really good.

00:42:50.316 --> 00:42:51.438
So we kind of booked it the wrong time,

00:42:51.438 --> 00:42:52.891
but it was amazing
weather, really good stuff

00:42:52.891 --> 00:42:53.724
on the last day.

00:42:53.724 --> 00:42:57.912
- I'm really, really impressed
that nobody got injured.

00:42:57.912 --> 00:42:59.958
'Cause there's six of us.

00:42:59.958 --> 00:43:02.606
I mean, did you guys take
any bad tumbles during--

00:43:02.606 --> 00:43:03.439
- Yeah.
- the ski trip?

00:43:03.439 --> 00:43:06.333
I let's just say I'm really
glad I rented outta a helmet.

00:43:06.333 --> 00:43:10.200
'Cause I think about 80%
of my falls involved me,

00:43:10.200 --> 00:43:12.885
just my head, just getting whiplash back.

00:43:12.885 --> 00:43:15.047
- Did you like kill a toddler Garnt?

00:43:15.047 --> 00:43:16.880
- I almost did.

00:43:16.880 --> 00:43:20.313
Because like on the first
like two, three days,

00:43:20.313 --> 00:43:21.675
I didn't know how to stop.

00:43:21.675 --> 00:43:26.582
So my technique for stopping
involved falling over

00:43:26.582 --> 00:43:27.870
and if I didn't fall over,

00:43:27.870 --> 00:43:29.337
I would just basically just take out

00:43:29.337 --> 00:43:30.794
whoever like was in front of me.

00:43:30.794 --> 00:43:33.840
- There's this great photo that
Luke took of you just like,

00:43:33.840 --> 00:43:36.143
there's this kid right here
and then there's just Garnt,

00:43:36.143 --> 00:43:40.090
menacingly behind me. Like
I'm about to destroy you.

00:43:40.090 --> 00:43:41.517
- Move out of the way.

00:43:41.517 --> 00:43:44.262
- So I must have decked
at least like three kids

00:43:44.262 --> 00:43:46.554
on the display from like
the past three days.

00:43:46.554 --> 00:43:49.383
- Oh my God, Garnt the kid killer.

00:43:49.383 --> 00:43:52.917
- Thank God no one got injured
except for those three kids.

00:43:52.917 --> 00:43:55.635
- None of us got injured.

00:43:55.635 --> 00:43:58.964
'Cause it was like a
competition because me and Luke

00:43:58.964 --> 00:44:02.040
just kept crashing into each
other on the first two days.

00:44:02.040 --> 00:44:03.590
'Cause we had zero control.

00:44:03.590 --> 00:44:05.008
We didn't know how to control our boards.

00:44:05.008 --> 00:44:07.675
And I remember Luke decked Joey, once.

00:44:07.675 --> 00:44:08.739
- Luke legs kicked me.

00:44:08.739 --> 00:44:11.072
- I had a great POV of this.

00:44:12.687 --> 00:44:15.178
I was like leading everyone
down the right slopes.

00:44:15.178 --> 00:44:17.235
And then I was waiting for
them bottom and I saw Joey

00:44:17.235 --> 00:44:20.402
just slowly like going down like this.

00:44:21.388 --> 00:44:22.886
And then out of nowhere, RKO,

00:44:22.886 --> 00:44:25.716
I just see our friend Luke
who doesn't know how to stop.

00:44:25.716 --> 00:44:29.423
- He's coming, coming and I
see Jerry. So, and I'm like,

00:44:29.423 --> 00:44:33.352
I'm about getting my popcorn
now waiting for this to happen.

00:44:33.352 --> 00:44:36.313
Joey's going, Joey's going,
doesn't move his head at all.

00:44:36.313 --> 00:44:38.119
And then suddenly he just goes, boom.

00:44:38.119 --> 00:44:41.784
Right in the back of his legs.
And Joey just flips over.

00:44:41.784 --> 00:44:43.267
Like that was so funny.

00:44:43.267 --> 00:44:46.494
- Because all I heard 'cause
I was slowly going down

00:44:46.494 --> 00:44:48.037
because it was kind of a narrow stretch.

00:44:48.037 --> 00:44:50.025
And also I was waiting for Luke.

00:44:50.025 --> 00:44:52.499
So I was slow going down
'cause I saw you guys there.

00:44:52.499 --> 00:44:54.730
And I remember specifically behind me,

00:44:54.730 --> 00:44:56.984
I could hear Luke in the distance going,

00:44:56.984 --> 00:44:59.402
"Sorry, sorry, sorry. Sorry."

00:44:59.402 --> 00:45:01.320
It's just getting louder
and louder and louder.

00:45:01.320 --> 00:45:03.622
But I thought he was
saying that to other people

00:45:03.622 --> 00:45:05.361
that were behind me.

00:45:05.361 --> 00:45:08.090
So I was like, oh Luke, silly him.

00:45:08.090 --> 00:45:08.938
- Silly him.

00:45:08.938 --> 00:45:11.609
- It gets louder. Sorry, sorry. Sorry.

00:45:11.609 --> 00:45:15.515
And then just bam right
in the back of my knees.

00:45:15.515 --> 00:45:17.731
- Let get fully over.

00:45:17.731 --> 00:45:19.611
- I should have been more
concerned, but it was so funny.

00:45:19.611 --> 00:45:22.116
- I wish you had filmed that.

00:45:22.116 --> 00:45:23.705
- By the time I realized it was happening,

00:45:23.705 --> 00:45:25.653
it was like five seconds.

00:45:25.653 --> 00:45:27.363
Couldn't have got my phone
out, but I wish I did.

00:45:27.363 --> 00:45:28.740
- I wanted to see your POV of that.

00:45:28.740 --> 00:45:30.912
- I wish I had my GoPro on permanently.

00:45:30.912 --> 00:45:33.650
- I was too busy with falling
over myself to really see

00:45:33.650 --> 00:45:35.622
what everyone else was falling over.

00:45:35.622 --> 00:45:37.571
'Cause I remember I had a few bad tumbles

00:45:37.571 --> 00:45:39.038
where actually some of the worst tumbles

00:45:39.038 --> 00:45:42.059
was when I was just actually
not going the fastest.

00:45:42.059 --> 00:45:45.165
It was like, cause when you go
fast, sometimes like you saw,

00:45:45.165 --> 00:45:47.518
you guys saw me do have
some pretty big falls

00:45:47.518 --> 00:45:50.684
where I did a triple back
flip or whatever or whatever.

00:45:50.684 --> 00:45:52.609
But to me, those falls are fine.

00:45:52.609 --> 00:45:54.233
'Cause you take the momentum

00:45:54.233 --> 00:45:56.744
and then you just literally roll with it.

00:45:56.744 --> 00:45:57.604
And you hardly feel it.

00:45:57.604 --> 00:46:00.806
Some of the worst falls I had
was on like the second day.

00:46:00.806 --> 00:46:01.686
- Think I saw this one.

00:46:01.686 --> 00:46:04.524
- These guys were trying to
warn me not to stop myself

00:46:04.524 --> 00:46:05.775
with my hands.

00:46:05.775 --> 00:46:07.762
Because sometimes if you have a bad fall,

00:46:07.762 --> 00:46:10.307
you stop yourself with your hands, you--

00:46:10.307 --> 00:46:11.182
- You snap your wrist.

00:46:11.182 --> 00:46:13.003
you could snap your wrist
or break your or something.

00:46:13.003 --> 00:46:15.830
So they were telling me,
you gotta fall on your arms.

00:46:15.830 --> 00:46:16.922
You gotta do this.

00:46:16.922 --> 00:46:18.544
Make sure you don't try to catch yourself.

00:46:18.544 --> 00:46:21.392
You gotta do this. And
like, like this, right?

00:46:21.392 --> 00:46:24.725
And I took that as I'm going to do this.

00:46:26.202 --> 00:46:29.697
Not realizing the mistake
I was about to encounter

00:46:29.697 --> 00:46:33.517
because what happened is I
was taking a bunch of tumbles.

00:46:33.517 --> 00:46:34.899
I was like, this doesn't hurt.

00:46:34.899 --> 00:46:38.019
I'm a pro at falling
over with a snowboard.

00:46:38.019 --> 00:46:41.280
So this one time I was going
down, this really like this,

00:46:41.280 --> 00:46:43.750
the slope wasn't steep at all.
I was going pretty slowly,

00:46:43.750 --> 00:46:46.425
but I just catched the
edge and I'm about to fall

00:46:46.425 --> 00:46:49.103
straight to my face. So
I do what they tell me.

00:46:49.103 --> 00:46:51.184
And I tuck my arms in.

00:46:51.184 --> 00:46:55.622
Unfortunately my fists were
right front of my face.

00:46:55.622 --> 00:47:00.622
So what happens is I fall on
my arm and I just deck myself

00:47:00.861 --> 00:47:02.583
in the face.

00:47:02.583 --> 00:47:06.250
I just go, which, and
I remember I fall over

00:47:09.266 --> 00:47:13.687
and when you have a bad fall
and you just gotta lay there.

00:47:13.687 --> 00:47:15.486
I just question life for a bit.

00:47:15.486 --> 00:47:17.233
- That's when you know it's bad.

00:47:17.233 --> 00:47:19.309
- And I remember I lay
there for a few seconds

00:47:19.309 --> 00:47:21.767
and I just hear kind of
going, "All right, Garnt."

00:47:21.767 --> 00:47:24.017
(laughing)

00:47:24.017 --> 00:47:25.293
- 'Cause I just saw this, like,

00:47:25.293 --> 00:47:26.962
'cause obviously it looks
like ants in the background.

00:47:26.962 --> 00:47:28.672
I just saw Garnt just fall on his face.

00:47:28.672 --> 00:47:30.788
And I was like, get back up, Garnt,

00:47:30.788 --> 00:47:32.633
get back up, get back up.

00:47:32.633 --> 00:47:34.706
And then he didn't get
up and I'm like, oh no,

00:47:34.706 --> 00:47:36.020
he hurt himself.

00:47:36.020 --> 00:47:38.681
- There was a couple
times on the last day,

00:47:38.681 --> 00:47:39.514
I think where you did that?

00:47:39.514 --> 00:47:40.799
Like triple back flip, right?

00:47:40.799 --> 00:47:43.203
I saw it in the distance and I was like,

00:47:43.203 --> 00:47:45.215
oh, that looked like it hurt.

00:47:45.215 --> 00:47:47.409
And then Garnt just didn't
move for about 20 seconds.

00:47:47.409 --> 00:47:48.625
I was like, oh he's dead.

00:47:48.625 --> 00:47:50.893
Oh he's straight up dead.

00:47:50.893 --> 00:47:52.243
- Yeah. I ever seen that one.

00:47:52.243 --> 00:47:54.378
I just saw like someone doing like flips

00:47:54.378 --> 00:47:55.211
but not the good type of flips.

00:47:55.211 --> 00:47:56.974
- I could hear the SSX music playing

00:47:56.974 --> 00:47:59.024
when that was happening.
It's like, let's drink.

00:47:59.024 --> 00:48:01.717
(all laughing)

00:48:01.717 --> 00:48:03.266
- You took so many falls.

00:48:03.266 --> 00:48:04.524
- I Did. I did.

00:48:04.524 --> 00:48:06.421
I think that's when I
learned the most though.

00:48:06.421 --> 00:48:08.019
when you do take the falls.

00:48:08.019 --> 00:48:10.054
- It's not about how many
times you get hit down.

00:48:10.054 --> 00:48:12.100
It's how many times you get back out.

00:48:12.100 --> 00:48:12.972
