01:17:40.785 --> 01:17:42.618
So time travel exists.

01:17:43.783 --> 01:17:46.283
So you're watching, you're
playing this perspective,

01:17:46.283 --> 01:17:48.862
this game from like 13
different perspectives.

01:17:48.862 --> 01:17:53.862
And these perspectives jump
between timelines and universes,

01:17:54.426 --> 01:17:59.426
depending on who you choose and
whose perspective you're on.

01:18:00.970 --> 01:18:03.975
And you think this will
be a complete mess.

01:18:03.975 --> 01:18:06.505
Like how can you tell a coherent
story when you can choose

01:18:06.505 --> 01:18:08.148
between 30 different perspectives?

01:18:08.148 --> 01:18:11.614
Well, how the game works is
that you can only progress

01:18:11.614 --> 01:18:15.404
to a certain amount of point
in one person's per perspective

01:18:15.404 --> 01:18:17.792
before you have to play
another person's perspective.

01:18:17.792 --> 01:18:21.916
So one person's story route
is unlocked by playing

01:18:21.916 --> 01:18:24.328
a certain part of another
person's story route.

01:18:24.328 --> 01:18:26.371
So the way you get delivered,

01:18:26.371 --> 01:18:28.997
the story is like little by
little and you get to piece

01:18:28.997 --> 01:18:33.997
together what has happened
between this entire timeline.

01:18:34.198 --> 01:18:35.237
